<title>GREECE: Greek CPI inflation falls to 7.5pct y/y in Dec.</title>
<headline>Greek CPI inflation falls to 7.5pct y/y in Dec.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1997-01-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Greek consumer price inflation dropped to 7.5 percent year-on-year in December from 7.7 percent in November, the National Statistics Service (NSS) said.</p>
<p>&quot;The prices of fish, beverages, housing and trasportation increased but the prices of fruits fell, NSS general secretary, Fani Zervou, told reporters.</p>
<p>    Consumer Price Index   December 96  November 96  December 95</p>
<p>    Month-on-month		 0.9%	 -0.3	    1.0%</p>
<p>    Yr-yr			    7.5%	  7.7%	   8.1%</p>
<p>    Index (1988=100)	   294.4	 291.8	  273.8</p>
<p>--Dimitris Kontogiannis, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
</text>
